  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q14-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Determine the range of $y=9-x^2$ and hence find the maximum value of $y$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Range: $y\\le 9$. Maximum value: $9$.",
          "worked": "Since $x^2\\ge 0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}-x^2&\\le 0\\\\9-x^2&\\le 9\\\\y&\\le 9.\\end{align*}$$\nEquality occurs at $x=0$, and $9-x^2$ has no lower bound. The range is $y\\le 9$, and the maximum value of $y$ is $9$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q14-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find the range of $f(x)=\\sqrt{9-x^2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0\\le y\\le 3$",
          "worked": "From part (a), $9-x^2\\le 9$. The square root is defined only when $9-x^2\\ge 0$, so\n$$\\begin{align*}0\\le 9-x^2&\\le 9\\\\0\\le \\sqrt{9-x^2}&\\le 3\\\\0\\le y&\\le 3.\\end{align*}$$\nThe endpoints are attained: $y=0$ at $x=\\pm3$, and $y=3$ at $x=0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q14-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Use a similar technique to find the range of $g(x)=\\sqrt{9+x^2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y\\ge 3$",
          "worked": "Since $x^2\\ge 0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}9+x^2&\\ge 9\\\\\\sqrt{9+x^2}&\\ge 3\\\\y&\\ge 3.\\end{align*}$$\nThe minimum is attained at $x=0$, and there is no upper bound. The range is $y\\ge 3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
